  "untestable": 0.1,
  "artifact": 0.1,
  "uncertain": 0.1
 },
 "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "The causal effect of a teammate DRIVE immediately preceding a PNR on the PNR's points per possession (PPP), controlling for relevant confounding factors.",
  "unit": "Individual offensive possession ending in a PNR.",
  "sample": "All PNR possessions from the NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, and 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, and the complete 2025-26 regular season. The 2025-26 playoffs will be included if complete when analysis begins. Possessions will be categorized based on whether a teammate DRIVE occurred immediately prior to the PNR within the same possession.",
  "power": "A power analysis will be conducted to determine the minimum detectable effect size, assuming a significance level (alpha) of 0.05 and a target power of 0.8. If the sample size for 'DRIVE preceding PNR' possessions is too small to detect a practically meaningful effect, the study will be re-evaluated for aggregation or scope reduction.",
  "controls": "Statistical controls will include: team offense/defense efficiency, game state (quarter, score differential, time remaining), PNR initiator and screener identity (player IDs), opponent defensive scheme (if available and reliable), and whether the possession originated from a turnover or offensive rebound. Fixed effects for team and season will also be considered. The definition of 'immediately preceding' will be operationalized as a DRIVE action occurring within 5 seconds and 2 actions prior to the PNR initiation within the same possession, without an intervening reset (e.g., shot attempt, turnover, dead ball).",
  "falsification": "A falsification test will involve analyzing the effect of a teammate DRIVE *following* a PNR on PNR PPP. If a significant positive effect is observed in this reverse-causal direction, it would suggest a potential issue with confounding or measurement, as a future event should not impact a past outcome.",
  "multiplicity": "No multiple testing corrections will be applied for the primary estimand. If secondary analyses (e.g., subgroup analyses by player, team, or specific types of PNRs) are conducted, appropriate adjustments (e.g., Bonferroni, Holm-Bonferroni, or False Discovery Rate) will be applied.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis 'Any teammate DRIVE preceding a PNR raises PNR PPP' will be considered supported if the estimated coefficient for the 'preceding DRIVE' indicator variable is statistically significant (p < 0.05) and positive in the primary regression model, after controlling for confounding factors. If the coefficient is not significant or is negative, the hypothesis will be rejected. If the sample size for the treatment group is too small to achieve useful power for a meaningful effect size, the outcome will be 'untestable'.",
  "data_version": "Play-by-play and derived play-type possession records from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 (complete regular season), as available on 2026-06-14."
 }
}

